  "custom_logic_notes": "The 'Rounding Candle' concept rounds the close price to the nearest _Point before comparing MA values. This means the MA values are computed on normally-close bars, but the signal comparison uses values derived from bar-close data. A trend filter using a separate pair of MAs (TrendPeriods, TrendPeriods+2) on a higher timeframe restricts entries to the prevailing trend direction. The DecreaseFactor serves dual purpose: when Lots>0 it reduces lot size after consecutive losses (money management recovery); when Lots<=0 it acts as the risk percentage for fractional position sizing. The trailing stop activates when price moves TrailingStop pips in profit and modifies SL to breakeven+gap.",
